# Driver 2 (USA) (Disc 1) SLUS-01161

[Increased Draw Distance]
Description = Increases the world draw distance from about 7 to 16 cells.
Author = Stenzek
Type = Gameshark
Activation = EndFrame
OverrideCPUOverclock = 300
; DrawMapPSX (8003F5A4) walks the 2048-unit map cells around the camera in a square spiral,
; visiting (0x1B9 >> goFaster) cells. goFaster is 1 in one-player mode, so only 220 cells
; (about 7 cells out) are considered. Cells with |h|+|v| >= 16 are also skipped, and each
; remaining cell is tested against the 21x21 PVS (potentially visible set) table, which only
; covers +/-10 cells and is indexed without bounds checks.
;
; This patch:
;   - Walks 0x882 >> 1 = 1089 cells (33x33, out to 16 cells), and raises the |h|+|v| limit to 23.
;     The existing 80000 back plane limit still trims the far corners.
;   - Replaces the PVS lookup with a code cave in unused BIOS RAM that clamps the cell offsets
;     to the table's +/-10 range, so cells past the edge inherit the visibility of the edge cell.
;   - Makes GetFirstPackedCop (800239E4) always check that a cell's map region is loaded, as it
;     already does in two-player mode. Only 2x2 regions of 32x32 cells are resident, so beyond
;     about 13 cells the slot may hold a different region. Those cells are now skipped instead of
;     being drawn from the wrong data.
; Two-player mode still uses its own shorter cell count.
AA00C000 00000018
